{% layout "default" %}

{% block content %}
  <div class="flex flex-col min-w-30 w-full">
    {% render "poll-title"
      , title: poll.title
      , remaining: null
      , poll: poll
      , admin: admin
      , localId: localId %}
    <p>The poll is ended. {{ results.total_voters | escape }} people answered. For each item, here's how the audience splits between wanting it, not minding, and not wanting it.</p>

    <ul class="flex flex-row flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-1 pl-0 my-2 text-sm list-none [&>li]:pl-0 [&>li]:my-0">
      <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="inline-block w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-teal-600"></span>Strongly want it</li>
      <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="inline-block w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-teal-800"></span>Want it</li>
      <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="inline-block w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-zinc-400"></span>Don't mind</li>
      <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="inline-block w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-orange-800"></span>Don't want it</li>
      <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="inline-block w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-orange-600"></span>Strongly don't want it</li>
      <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="inline-block w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-zinc-700"></span>Unclear answer</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 my-0 w-full">
      {% for entry in results.features %}
        {% assign want = entry.shares.want | times: 100 | round %}
        {% assign meh = entry.shares.indifferent | times: 100 | round %}
        {% assign reject = entry.shares.reject | times: 100 | round %}
        {% assign unclear = entry.shares.unclear | times: 100 | round %}
        {% assign strong_want = entry.intensity.strong_want | times: 100 | round %}
        {% assign mild_want = entry.intensity.mild_want | times: 100 | round %}
        {% assign mild_reject = entry.intensity.mild_reject | times: 100 | round %}
        {% assign strong_reject = entry.intensity.strong_reject | times: 100 | round %}
        {% assign margin = entry.margin | times: 100 | round %}
        <section class="flex flex-col gap-2 px-6 py-4 my-0 w-full text-zinc-200 bg-sky-700 rounded-xl">
          <h3 class="my-0 text-lg text-zinc-100">{{ entry.name | escape }}</h3>

          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-zinc-50 leading-tight">{{ entry.verdict.headline | escape }}</div>
          {% if entry.verdict.detail != '' %}
            <p class="my-0 text-sm text-zinc-200">{{ entry.verdict.detail | escape }}</p>
          {% endif %}

          {% if entry.responses > 0 %}
            <div
              class="flex flex-row w-full h-7 mt-1 gap-[2px] p-[2px] rounded-md bg-sky-900 text-xs font-bold text-zinc-50 [&>div]:flex [&>div]:items-center [&>div]:justify-center [&>div]:overflow-hidden [&>div]:rounded"
              role="img"
              aria-label="{{ want }}% want it ({{ strong_want }}% strongly), {{ meh }}% don't mind, {{ reject }}% don't want it ({{ strong_reject }}% strongly), {{ unclear }}% unclear">
              {% if entry.intensity.strong_want > 0 %}
                <div class="bg-teal-600" style="width: {{ entry.intensity.strong_want | times: 100 }}%" title="Strongly want it: {{ strong_want }}%">{% if strong_want >= 8 %}{{ strong_want }}%{% endif %}</div>
              {% endif %}
              {% if entry.intensity.mild_want > 0 %}
                <div class="bg-teal-800" style="width: {{ entry.intensity.mild_want | times: 100 }}%" title="Want it: {{ mild_want }}%">{% if mild_want >= 8 %}{{ mild_want }}%{% endif %}</div>
              {% endif %}
              {% if entry.shares.indifferent > 0 %}
                <div class="bg-zinc-400 text-zinc-900" style="width: {{ entry.shares.indifferent | times: 100 }}%" title="Don't mind: {{ meh }}%">{% if meh >= 8 %}{{ meh }}%{% endif %}</div>
              {% endif %}
              {% if entry.intensity.mild_reject > 0 %}
                <div class="bg-orange-800" style="width: {{ entry.intensity.mild_reject | times: 100 }}%" title="Don't want it: {{ mild_reject }}%">{% if mild_reject >= 8 %}{{ mild_reject }}%{% endif %}</div>
              {% endif %}
              {% if entry.intensity.strong_reject > 0 %}
                <div class="bg-orange-600" style="width: {{ entry.intensity.strong_reject | times: 100 }}%" title="Strongly don't want it: {{ strong_reject }}%">{% if strong_reject >= 8 %}{{ strong_reject }}%{% endif %}</div>
              {% endif %}
              {% if entry.shares.unclear > 0 %}
                <div class="bg-zinc-700" style="width: {{ entry.shares.unclear | times: 100 }}%" title="Unclear: {{ unclear }}%">{% if unclear >= 8 %}{{ unclear }}%{% endif %}</div>
              {% endif %}
            </div>

            <div class="flex flex-row flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 mt-1 text-sm text-zinc-300">
              <span>
                Overall: <b class="text-zinc-100">{{ entry.category_plain | escape }}</b> — {{ entry.category_meaning | escape }}
                {% unless entry.category_clear or entry.small_sample %}
                  {% if entry.category_runner_up %}
                    <span class="text-zinc-200">— close call with {{ entry.category_runner_up_plain | escape }}</span>
                  {% endif %}
                {% endunless %}
              </span>
              {% if entry.small_sample %}
                <span class="ml-auto whitespace-nowrap">{{ entry.responses }} {% if entry.responses == 1 %}response{% else %}responses{% endif %} · too few to be reliable</span>
              {% else %}
                <span class="ml-auto whitespace-nowrap">{{ entry.responses }} responses · ±{{ margin }}%</span>
              {% endif %}
            </div>
          {% endif %}
        </section>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <details class="mt-6 text-sm">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer">How to read this</summary>
    <ul>
      <li>Everyone answered two questions per item: how they'd feel <i>with</i> it and how they'd feel <i>without</i> it. Each pair of answers puts that person in one bucket: <b>want it</b> (they'd be happier with it or miss it if gone), <b>don't mind</b>, <b>don't want it</b> (they'd rather it were gone), or <b>unclear</b> (contradictory answers).</li>
      <li>The <b>±</b> figure is the margin of error at this many responses (95% confidence, Wilson score interval). If the "want it" and "don't want it" ranges overlap, the poll can't tell them apart — the verdict says so. Under {{ small_sample }} responses no margin is shown, because at that size the real shares could be almost anything.</li>
      <li>The vivid ends of the bar are people who felt <b>strongly</b> — 😍 to one question <i>and</i> 😡 to the other. The dimmer parts are one-sided: they'd enjoy it but not miss it, or miss it but not be excited by it (and likewise for not wanting it). Two long vivid ends means a genuinely polarized audience; long dim ends means a split that nobody feels strongly about.</li>
      <li><b>Overall</b> sums up the most common kind of answer for the item. The first three all count as "want it" on the bar — they differ in <i>how</i> it's wanted: <i>Taken for granted</i> — not exciting to have, but missed if it went; <i>Wanted</i> — happier with it, unhappy without it; <i>Bonus</i> — enjoyed when present, not missed when gone. Then <i>Doesn't matter</i> — few people care either way; <i>Better without</i> — people would rather not have it; <i>Mixed signals</i> — answers contradict each other. "Close call" means the runner-up was within noise of the winner.</li>
      <li>Raw counts per item (must-be / performance / attractive / indifferent / reverse / questionable):
        {% for entry in results.features %}
          <br><span class="text-zinc-400">{{ entry.name | escape }}: M {{ entry.counts.M }} · O {{ entry.counts.O }} · A {{ entry.counts.A }} · I {{ entry.counts.I }} · R {{ entry.counts.R }} · Q {{ entry.counts.Q }}</span>
        {% endfor %}
      </li>
    </ul>
  </details>
{% endblock %}
